    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file `extract_json.py` that calls a hosted LLM to extract structured JSON from text, I need to choose a concrete external provider. I will use Amazon Bedrock for this task as it is a well-known service that provides access to various LLMs. The code will import the necessary SDK and use a specific model identifier to make it identifiable. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789849044894,
          "start": 1789849042580
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb50fe940010hVEL3Q51TSmIi",
