    },
    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the `summarize_text.py` file that calls a hosted LLM to summarize long text, I will use the Amazon Bedrock service, which is a concrete external provider. I will import the necessary SDK and use the specific model identifier to make the provider identifiable in the code. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789849039111,
          "start": 1789849036320
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bb50e620001Y0b1x6m31mKP1a",
